{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "00143",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 0.93,
      "end_seconds": 3.04,
      "duration_seconds": 2.11,
      "text": "Right, come in and get settled."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 3.71,
      "end_seconds": 6.57,
      "duration_seconds": 2.86,
      "text": "Okay, so hello, doctor, thank you."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 7.81,
      "end_seconds": 10.03,
      "duration_seconds": 2.22,
      "text": "Tell me what's been troubling you."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 11.52,
      "end_seconds": 21.7,
      "duration_seconds": 10.18,
      "text": "I've been dealing with severe pain in my right side that comes in waves. It's a relief to finally sit down and talk about it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 22.22,
      "end_seconds": 24.47,
      "duration_seconds": 2.25,
      "text": "When did you first notice it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 25.26,
      "end_seconds": 36.8,
      "duration_seconds": 11.54,
      "text": "It's, It's been like this since last Tuesday. My sister suggested writing things down, but I forgot. I didn't want to make a fuss, you know."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 37.24,
      "end_seconds": 48.56,
      "duration_seconds": 11.32,
      "text": "Can you describe it a bit more for me? How strong it is, what the pattern is, what helps. Bear with me, I'm just building up the picture."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 49.29,
      "end_seconds": 63.78,
      "duration_seconds": 14.49,
      "text": "It's a few times a day. It's moderate, honestly. Right, I've had pain moving down to the groin too, for two weeks. I've, I've also had restlessness, I can't sit still."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 67.69,
      "end_seconds": 81.45,
      "duration_seconds": 13.76,
      "text": "Let me explain how I'm thinking about this. When someone has symptoms like these, we first look for the common and treatable causes, and only then for the rarer ones. That's why I'm going step by step rather than ordering everything at once."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 82.57,
      "end_seconds": 84.35,
      "duration_seconds": 1.78,
      "text": "Okay, that makes sense."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 84.74,
      "end_seconds": 88.59,
      "duration_seconds": 3.85,
      "text": "Have you had any difficulty passing urine, vomiting or testicular pain?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 89.49,
      "end_seconds": 91.25,
      "duration_seconds": 1.76,
      "text": "Nothing like that, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 91.88,
      "end_seconds": 94.07,
      "duration_seconds": 2.19,
      "text": "Any problems with your joints or muscles?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 94.47,
      "end_seconds": 96.44,
      "duration_seconds": 1.97,
      "text": "No, joints are fine."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 97.55,
      "end_seconds": 100.06,
      "duration_seconds": 2.51,
      "text": "Did you manage to eat before coming?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 101.31,
      "end_seconds": 105.38,
      "duration_seconds": 4.07,
      "text": "Yeah, yes, I had something small this morning."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 106.14,
      "end_seconds": 109.3,
      "duration_seconds": 3.16,
      "text": "Anyone in the family with similar problems or other conditions?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 110.51,
      "end_seconds": 112.58,
      "duration_seconds": 2.07,
      "text": "My sister has thyroid problems."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 113.5,
      "end_seconds": 116.83,
      "duration_seconds": 3.33,
      "text": "Let me just pull up your file for a second."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 117.63,
      "end_seconds": 118.33,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Sure."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 127.29,
      "end_seconds": 131.23,
      "duration_seconds": 3.94,
      "text": "Okay, here we go. What medicines are you taking at the moment?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 131.59,
      "end_seconds": 135.08,
      "duration_seconds": 3.49,
      "text": "It's allopurinol, once a day for the gout."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 135.92,
      "end_seconds": 137.59,
      "duration_seconds": 1.67,
      "text": "Do you know the dose?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 138.86,
      "end_seconds": 146.49,
      "duration_seconds": 7.63,
      "text": "100 milligrams, I think that's what's on the box. It's losartan, 50 milligrams, once a day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 148.06,
      "end_seconds": 161.38,
      "duration_seconds": 13.32,
      "text": "I'll be straight with you about how this works. Most of what we see in clinic turns out to be manageable, and the history you give me is often more useful than any single test, so thank you for being so detailed."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 162.49,
      "end_seconds": 165.5,
      "duration_seconds": 3.01,
      "text": "Oh, thank you, that really helps."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 166.69,
      "end_seconds": 170.78,
      "duration_seconds": 4.09,
      "text": "What about your general health, any conditions you're being treated for?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 171.91,
      "end_seconds": 186.22,
      "duration_seconds": 14.31,
      "text": "I've had gout for five years now. I just want to get back to normal, really. High blood pressure, for nearly five years. I'm not great at remembering details, so bear with me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 186.53,
      "end_seconds": 199.48,
      "duration_seconds": 12.95,
      "text": "Alright. Okay, gout, that's already on your record. Good to know. Right, so that's your known high blood pressure. We'll keep that in mind today. Alright, how's everything else at home otherwise?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 200.69,
      "end_seconds": 207.73,
      "duration_seconds": 7.04,
      "text": "Busy. Everyone's running in different directions at the moment, uh, you know how it is."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 209.0,
      "end_seconds": 212.26,
      "duration_seconds": 3.26,
      "text": "What about allergies, to medicines or foods or anything else?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 212.61,
      "end_seconds": 216.61,
      "duration_seconds": 4.0,
      "text": "Hmm, no, none that I know of."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 218.07,
      "end_seconds": 220.41,
      "duration_seconds": 2.34,
      "text": "One moment, the system's being slow today."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 220.72,
      "end_seconds": 221.57,
      "duration_seconds": 0.85,
      "text": "That's alright."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 229.37,
      "end_seconds": 230.78,
      "duration_seconds": 1.41,
      "text": "Right, thanks for waiting."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 232.37,
      "end_seconds": 238.29,
      "duration_seconds": 5.92,
      "text": "Doctor, I've got the readings for you. Blood pressure 122 over 80, temperature 36.7, pulse 112."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 239.4,
      "end_seconds": 251.57,
      "duration_seconds": 12.17,
      "text": "Thanks. I like to make sure you understand what's happening, so please stop me at any point. There are no silly questions, and I'd much rather you ask now than go home still wondering about something."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 252.39,
      "end_seconds": 254.2,
      "duration_seconds": 1.81,
      "text": "Right, I understand now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 255.94,
      "end_seconds": 258.42,
      "duration_seconds": 2.48,
      "text": "Let me have a look at you now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 260.04,
      "end_seconds": 261.69,
      "duration_seconds": 1.65,
      "text": "Let me check your reflexes."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 274.69,
      "end_seconds": 279.79,
      "duration_seconds": 5.1,
      "text": "There's tenderness in the right loin when I tap, and your tummy is soft."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 280.96,
      "end_seconds": 282.95,
      "duration_seconds": 1.99,
      "text": "Yes, you know, doctor."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 287.13,
      "end_seconds": 300.24,
      "duration_seconds": 13.11,
      "text": "Right, that's fine, you can get dressed. Thanks for bearing with me. Now that I've had a look, I can put the whole picture together. Have you been able to keep up with your usual activities?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 301.56,
      "end_seconds": 316.18,
      "duration_seconds": 14.62,
      "text": "For the most part, uh, yes. I just carry on and try not to dwell on things too much, though I won't pretend it hasn't crossed my mind a few times."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 316.52,
      "end_seconds": 326.7,
      "duration_seconds": 10.18,
      "text": "So, based on the history and the examination, my working impression is a kidney stone. I want to be honest that this is an impression, not a final answer."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 327.48,
      "end_seconds": 329.33,
      "duration_seconds": 1.85,
      "text": "Doctor, is this dangerous?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 330.25,
      "end_seconds": 349.77,
      "duration_seconds": 19.52,
      "text": "It's reasonable to be concerned, but right now a kidney stone is my leading thought, not anything worse. Let me just recap so I've got it right. You've had severe pain in your right side that comes in waves, since last Tuesday, moderate, and no difficulty passing urine or vomiting."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0048",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 350.97,
      "end_seconds": 353.72,
      "duration_seconds": 2.75,
      "text": "Right, exactly, that's what's been happening."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0049",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 354.67,
      "end_seconds": 358.03,
      "duration_seconds": 3.36,
      "text": "Sorry about the noise outside, the building work never stops."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0050",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 359.48,
      "end_seconds": 361.87,
      "duration_seconds": 2.39,
      "text": "I hadn't even noticed, honestly."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0051",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 362.64,
      "end_seconds": 379.31,
      "duration_seconds": 16.67,
      "text": "I'd like to arrange a CT scan of the kidneys and bladder for suspected renal colic. I'd like you to take diclofenac, 50 milligrams, twice a day after food, for three days. That should help with stone pain. I'll put all of this in writing so you don't have to remember it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0052",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 380.09,
      "end_seconds": 398.26,
      "duration_seconds": 18.17,
      "text": "I'd like you to take paracetamol, 1 gram, every six hours if needed, for three days. That should help with pain. It's a commonly used medicine and most people tolerate it well. Drink three litres of water a day and try to strain your urine so we can catch the stone if it passes."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0053",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 398.77,
      "end_seconds": 417.27,
      "duration_seconds": 18.5,
      "text": "I see. Please take the tablets with food so they don't upset your stomach. Don't skip meals, and try to eat smaller portions more often through the day. If you get a fever or can't pass urine at all, or you feel really unwell, please don't wait, come to the emergency department."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0054",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 420.12,
      "end_seconds": 423.05,
      "duration_seconds": 2.93,
      "text": "Yes, uh, I'll do that."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0055",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 424.48,
      "end_seconds": 427.37,
      "duration_seconds": 2.89,
      "text": "Please come and see me in a week."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0056",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 428.51,
      "end_seconds": 433.61,
      "duration_seconds": 5.1,
      "text": "Hmm, sure, I'll make the appointment on the way out."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0057",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 434.89,
      "end_seconds": 438.83,
      "duration_seconds": 3.94,
      "text": "Just to confirm, what are the next steps as you understand them?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0058",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 439.68,
      "end_seconds": 450.87,
      "duration_seconds": 11.19,
      "text": "So, I take the diclofenac, 50 milligrams, twice a day after food and take the paracetamol, 1 gram, every six hours if needed. Is that right?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0059",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 451.17,
      "end_seconds": 455.84,
      "duration_seconds": 4.67,
      "text": "Alright, yes, exactly right. I think we've covered it. Do you have any questions?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0060",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 456.15,
      "end_seconds": 459.42,
      "duration_seconds": 3.27,
      "text": "That's all, thank you for your time."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0061",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 460.59,
      "end_seconds": 461.64,
      "duration_seconds": 1.05,
      "text": "See you then."
    }
  ]
}